1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,680
You say the word Amen. You shout Hallelujah.

2
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:05,140
Both Hebrew. You plan your week in seven days

3
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:06,600
with one day of rest.

4
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:08,440
That rhythm comes from the Hebrew Bible.

5
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:11,040
Christmas, built around a Jewish teacher.

6
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:13,680
Your map app, Waze, was built by Israelis.

7
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:17,200
Your laptop's processor may have been designed in Haifa.

8
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:18,840
Now here's the strange part.

9
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:21,840
All of it came from a people who for nearly 2,000 years

10
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:25,320
had no country at all, scattered across every continent,

11
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:27,120
expelled again and again.

12
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:30,000
Then in 1948, they had one.

13
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,560
A land the size of New Jersey,

14
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:34,320
and nearly everyone on earth has an opinion about it.

15
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:36,320
Almost nobody has the whole story.

16
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:37,680
So where does it begin?

17
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:41,000
4,000 years ago in a hot dry land called Canaan.

18
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,520
And why does it still burn?

19
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:45,560
4,000 years, 30 minutes.

20
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:47,960
Each side's story, told fairly.

21
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:48,840
Let's go.

22
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:50,520
Start with a man named Abraham.

23
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:51,360
According to the Bible,

24
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:53,080
he leaves his home in Mesopotamia

25
00:00:53,080 --> 00:00:55,000
and walks west into Canaan.

26
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,080
The land between the Mediterranean Sea and the Jordan River.

27
00:00:58,080 --> 00:01:00,720
His grandson Jacob is renamed Israel,

28
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:04,040
which means something like he who struggles with God.

29
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,720
Jacob's twelve sons become the twelve tribes.

30
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:08,520
Famine drives the family to Egypt

31
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:10,840
and the story says they are enslaved there

32
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:13,120
until a leader named Moses brings them out

33
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:15,360
and at Mount Sinai they receive the law.

34
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:17,520
Historians can't confirm that story.

35
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:19,920
There is no Egyptian record of an Exodus,

36
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:22,160
but there is one very old clue.

37
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:24,240
Around 1208 BCE,

38
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,840
the Egyptian pharaoh Merneptah carved a victory stone

39
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:30,200
listing the peoples he had crushed in Canaan.

40
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:32,120
One of them is called Israel.

41
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:35,000
It's the oldest known mention of the name outside the Bible.

42
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,920
So about 3,200 years ago,

43
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:41,280
someone called Israel was already living in those hills.

44
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:43,080
By around 1,000 BCE,

45
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:46,000
the Bible says the tribes unite under kings.

46
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:47,640
First Saul, then David,

47
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:49,760
who captures a hill town called Jerusalem

48
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:51,120
and makes it his capital.

49
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:53,240
His son Solomon builds a great temple there,

50
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:54,480
the first temple.

51
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:56,520
How big was this kingdom really?

52
00:01:56,520 --> 00:01:58,520
Archaeologists argue about it.

53
00:01:58,520 --> 00:02:00,240
Some see an empire.

54
00:02:00,240 --> 00:02:02,600
Others see a small highland kingdom.

55
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:05,240
What nobody argues about is what the temple did.

56
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:08,400
It made Jerusalem the center of Jewish life for good.

57
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:10,680
After Solomon, the kingdom splits in two.

58
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:14,000
Israel in the north, Judah in the south with Jerusalem.

59
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,000
In these years, prophets like Amos and Isaiah appear,

60
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,240
denouncing kings who ignore the poor

61
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:22,440
and demanding justice from the powerful.

62
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:25,640
Those demands become some of the most quoted words in the Bible,

63
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:27,640
but the neighborhood gets dangerous.

64
00:02:27,640 --> 00:02:31,440
In 722 BCE, the Assyrian Empire crushes the northern kingdom

65
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:32,880
and scatters its people.

66
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:35,720
They vanish from history, the 10 lost tribes,

67
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:38,760
Judah survives, barely. Then comes Babylon.

68
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:42,600
In 586 BCE, King Nebuchadnezzar burns Jerusalem,

69
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:43,880
destroys Solomon's temple

70
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:48,320
and marches Judah's leaders almost 1,000 miles east in chains.

71
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:49,720
That is the first exile.

72
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:51,040
And it changes everything.

73
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:53,720
Here's the question exile forces.

74
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:56,040
If your god lives in one temple in one city

75
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:58,600
and the temple is rubble and you're 1,000 miles away,

76
00:02:58,600 --> 00:02:59,760
what are you?

77
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:03,000
The exiles in Babylon answer by inventing something new.

78
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,000
They gather.

79
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,600
They write down their stories.

80
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:08,120
They pray together without any temple at all.

81
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:10,840
A people held together by a book and a calendar,

82
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:12,200
instead of a building.

83
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:13,320
Remember that.

84
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:16,000
It's the trick that will save them again and again.

85
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,240
In 539 BCE, Persia conquers Babylon

86
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:21,400
and King Cyrus lets the exiles go home.

87
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:23,040
Some go, many stay.

88
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:25,280
The ones who return build a second temple

89
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:26,600
and for the next few centuries,

90
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:30,000
Judea is a small province under one empire after another.

91
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:33,520
First Persia, then in 332, Alexander the Great

92
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:37,480
and after him, Greek language, Greek gods and Greek gyms.

93
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:39,800
Which brings us to a king named Antiochus,

94
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:42,920
who in 167 BCE bans Jewish practice

95
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:44,480
and sets up an idol in the temple

96
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:47,880
a family called the Maccabees rebels, and wins.

97
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:50,240
They rededicate the temple. That is Hanukkah,

98
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:51,560
the festival of lights.

99
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:53,000
And for roughly 80 years,

100
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,040
the Jews have their own kingdom again.

101
00:03:55,040 --> 00:03:56,080
Then Rome arrives.

102
00:03:56,080 --> 00:04:00,240
In 63 BCE, the general Pompey marches into Jerusalem.

103
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:02,280
Rome backs a king named Herod,

104
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:04,400
who rebuilds the temple on a spectacular scale.

105
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:07,440
The huge stones of its retaining wall still stand today.

106
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:08,560
It's the Western wall.

107
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:12,600
Under Rome, Judea simmers, taxes, rebels, rival sects.

108
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:14,440
One of them gathers around a Jewish teacher

109
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:16,000
from Galilee named Jesus,

110
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:19,720
who is executed by Roman authority around the year 30.

111
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:21,360
His followers start a movement

112
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:24,320
that will much later become Christianity.

113
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:27,480
In 66 CE, the Jews rise up against Rome.

114
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:29,240
It is a catastrophe.

115
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:32,680
In 70, the Roman general Titus besieges Jerusalem

116
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:34,480
and burns the second temple.

117
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:36,000
Hundreds of thousands die.

118
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,000
The arch of Titus in Rome, still standing,

119
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:40,920
shows soldiers carrying off the temple's golden menorah.

120
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:44,080
The last rebels hold out in the desert fortress of Masada

121
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:45,680
until about 73.

122
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:47,440
Hope flares one more time.

123
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:51,200
In 132, a leader named Simon bar Kokhba revolts again.

124
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:54,560
Rome crushes it by 135 at terrible cost.

125
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:57,360
The emperor Hadrian bans Jews from Jerusalem

126
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:59,960
and renames the province Syria Palaestina.

127
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:01,920
The name that Palestine comes from.

128
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:04,720
So now the people have no temple, no capital,

129
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:07,320
and in most of the land, no permission to live there.

130
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:08,440
What do they have?

131
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:10,640
The book, over the next few centuries,

132
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:12,800
rabbis in Galilee and in Babylon,

133
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:14,080
write down their traditions,

134
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:16,120
the Mishnah, then the Talmud,

135
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:18,200
a nation packed into a library,

136
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:20,400
and a library can travel anywhere.

137
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:23,120
Meanwhile, the little movement around Jesus grows

138
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:26,040
and slowly splits away from Judaism.

139
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:27,600
In the early 300s,

140
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:30,600
the Roman emperor Constantine embraces Christianity.

141
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:32,040
And within about 70 years,

142
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:34,240
it is the empire's official religion.

143
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:36,200
Now the land that Jews are barred from

144
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:37,720
is a Christian holy land,

145
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:40,880
with great churches rising over the places of the gospels.

146
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:43,600
For Jews, the next centuries bring new bans,

147
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:46,120
forced conversions, and revolts that fail.

148
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:49,480
But the book keeps them together, the diaspora.

149
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:51,280
For about 1800 years,

150
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:54,040
most Jews live as a minority somewhere else.

151
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:56,880
After 638, many live under Islamic rule,

152
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:58,640
which takes Jerusalem that year.

153
00:05:58,640 --> 00:06:01,960
Jews and Christians there are protected but second class.

154
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:04,560
They pay a special tax and live under rules.

155
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:07,280
Sometimes that is mild, sometimes it isn't.

156
00:06:07,280 --> 00:06:09,600
But compared with what's coming in Christian Europe,

157
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:11,120
it is often calmer.

158
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:14,640
In Muslim Spain, in the 10th and 11th centuries,

159
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:17,920
Jewish poets, doctors, and philosophers flourish.

160
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:20,600
Maimonides, born in Córdoba in 1138,

161
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:24,320
becomes the most influential Jewish thinker of the Middle Ages

162
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:26,480
and a physician at the court in Cairo.

163
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:29,720
Meanwhile in Christian Europe, the pressure builds.

164
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:32,640
In 1099, Crusaders captured Jerusalem

165
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:35,000
and slaughter Muslims and Jews alike.

166
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:35,880
On the way,

167
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:39,160
Crusader mobs massacred Jewish communities along the Rhine.

168
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:42,000
Jews are barred from owning land and joining guilds.

169
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:43,640
So many become money lenders,

170
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:46,000
work that Christians are forbidden to do

171
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,480
and are then hated for it.

172
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:50,240
Lies spread that Jews poison wells

173
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:52,800
that they murder Christian children for ritual blood.

174
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:55,800
None of it is true and thousands die because of it.

175
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:59,920
Then the expulsions, England, 1290, France, 1306,

176
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:03,720
and Spain, 1492, the same year Columbus sails.

177
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:05,560
The Alhambra decree gives Spain's Jews

178
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:07,720
a few months to convert or leave.

179
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:10,720
Tens of thousands go by some estimates far more.

180
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:13,280
The Ottoman Sultan welcomes many of them.

181
00:07:13,280 --> 00:07:16,640
They carry their Spanish with them, a language called Ladino.

182
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:19,480
And in 1516, the city of Venice does something

183
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:21,160
that gives the world a word.

184
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:24,720
It orders all its Jews to live on one small island

185
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:27,360
beside an old foundry locked in at night.

186
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:29,640
The island is called the Ghetto.

187
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:33,000
The word spreads across Europe and so do the walls.

188
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,320
In Eastern Europe, Poland takes in Jews

189
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:37,720
and by the 1800s, most of the world's Jews

190
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:40,800
live under the Russian Empire, held inside a zone

191
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:42,400
called the Pale of Settlement.

192
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:44,680
Then, in the age of the French Revolution,

193
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:47,120
a new door opens, emancipation.

194
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:49,120
Citizenship for Jews first in France,

195
00:07:49,120 --> 00:07:51,800
then across the West, Jews pour into universities

196
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:52,960
and professions.

197
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:54,680
But a new hatred arrives with it,

198
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:58,360
based not on religion, but on invented ideas of race.

199
00:07:58,360 --> 00:08:01,640
And in Russia, in 1881, after the Tsar is assassinated,

200
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:03,160
pogroms sweep the country.

201
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:05,760
Mobs burning, killing, year after year.

202
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:09,400
Millions of Jews emigrate mostly to America.

203
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:10,880
A few thousand go somewhere else.

204
00:08:10,880 --> 00:08:12,960
Their ancient homeland, then a quiet corner

205
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:14,080
of the Ottoman Empire.

206
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:18,160
In 1894, a French army officer named Alfred Dreyfus,

207
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:20,840
a Jew, is falsely convicted of treason.

208
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:23,360
A journalist named Theodor Herzl covers the case

209
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:25,760
for a Vienna newspaper and it shakes him.

210
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:28,680
If this can happen in France, the most enlightened country

211
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:32,280
in Europe, he decides, then Jews will never be safe

212
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:34,000
as a minority anywhere.

213
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:37,920
In 1896, he writes a pamphlet called the Jewish State.

214
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:40,560
In 1897, he holds the first Zionist Congress

215
00:08:40,560 --> 00:08:42,240
in Basel, Switzerland.

216
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:45,160
The idea is simple, Jews need a country of their own.

217
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:48,560
Zionism named for Zion, a hill in Jerusalem.

218
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:51,120
Many religious and many secular Jews at first

219
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:53,640
think it's absurd or dangerous.

220
00:08:53,640 --> 00:08:56,640
But the pogroms keep coming and the idea spreads.

221
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:59,640
A scholar named Eliezer Ben Yehuda moves to Jerusalem

222
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:01,600
and attempts something almost unheard of,

223
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:04,120
reviving Hebrew as an everyday spoken language,

224
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:08,120
after nearly 2,000 years as a language of prayer and books.

225
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:10,360
He raises his son speaking only Hebrew.

226
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:11,960
People think he's mad.

227
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:14,080
Today, millions of Israelis speak it.

228
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:18,960
The first wave of settlers arrives in 1882, mostly from Russia.

229
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:21,200
They drain swamps, plant vineyards,

230
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:22,840
and found farming villages,

231
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:26,160
some funded by the banker Baron Edmond de Rothschild.

232
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:29,640
In 1909, a group founds the first kibbutz, Degania,

233
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:32,840
and another founds a sandy suburb of Jaffa called Tel Aviv

234
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:34,160
to the Arab farmers nearby,

235
00:09:34,160 --> 00:09:36,600
the newcomers are strangers buying up land.

236
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:39,280
Some trade with them, some resent them,

237
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:41,160
few yet see what is coming.

238
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:45,640
By 1914, a few tens of thousands of Jews live in Ottoman Palestine

239
00:09:45,640 --> 00:09:50,000
alongside about 600,000 Arabs, Muslim and Christian,

240
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:52,400
whose families have been there for centuries.

241
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:54,720
And that is where the story gets complicated.

242
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:57,280
Because now, two peoples claim one land.

243
00:09:57,280 --> 00:09:59,600
World War I breaks the Ottoman Empire.

244
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:01,320
And Britain takes Palestine.

245
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:04,600
During the war, London makes promises that can't all be kept.

246
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:07,200
To Arab leaders, promises of independence.

247
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:11,320
And in November 1917, in the Balfour Declaration,

248
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:12,840
a letter of a few lines.

249
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:14,320
Britain views with favor,

250
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:16,800
a national home for the Jewish people in Palestine.

251
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:18,600
Provided nothing harms the rights

252
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:20,840
of the existing non-Jewish communities.

253
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:22,280
Jews cheer.

254
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:25,080
Arabs, then about nine in 10 of the people there,

255
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:28,120
see a foreign power promising away their country.

256
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:31,520
In the 1920s and 30s, Jewish immigration rises

257
00:10:31,520 --> 00:10:34,400
from Poland and after Hitler from Germany.

258
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:37,520
Tel Aviv grows from a sand-dune suburb into a city.

259
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:38,640
Kibbutzim spread.

260
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:41,200
Land is bought often from absent landlords

261
00:10:41,200 --> 00:10:44,400
and sometimes the Arab farmers who worked it are evicted.

262
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:46,040
Take 1929.

263
00:10:46,040 --> 00:10:48,400
A dispute over access to the Western Wall

264
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:50,640
explodes into riots across Palestine.

265
00:10:50,640 --> 00:10:54,240
In Hebron, Arab mobs kill 67 Jews.

266
00:10:54,240 --> 00:10:56,600
And the survivors are driven out of a Jewish community

267
00:10:56,600 --> 00:10:58,640
that had lived there for centuries.

268
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:01,040
More than 100 Arabs are killed too,

269
00:11:01,040 --> 00:11:03,760
most of them by British police and troops.

270
00:11:03,760 --> 00:11:05,800
Trust between the communities shrinks.

271
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:09,120
By 1936, with the Jewish share of the population

272
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:10,760
more than a quarter and rising,

273
00:11:10,760 --> 00:11:13,800
Palestinian Arabs launch a revolt against both Britain

274
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:15,480
and Jewish settlement.

275
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:18,040
Britain crushes it, killing thousands.

276
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:20,400
Jewish militias, the Haganah,

277
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:22,680
and the more militant Irgun fight back

278
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:25,040
and sometimes attack Arab civilians.

279
00:11:25,040 --> 00:11:29,080
Violence from both sides is already part of the story.

280
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:31,480
In the middle of the revolt in 1937,

281
00:11:31,480 --> 00:11:33,880
a British commission, the Peel Commission,

282
00:11:33,880 --> 00:11:37,120
concludes that the two peoples cannot share one government

283
00:11:37,120 --> 00:11:39,520
and proposes the first partition plan,

284
00:11:39,520 --> 00:11:42,320
a small Jewish state and a larger Arab one.

285
00:11:42,320 --> 00:11:45,520
Most Zionist leaders accept the principle with doubts.

286
00:11:45,520 --> 00:11:48,120
Arab leaders reject it, nothing happens.

287
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:51,240
Then in May 1939, as war looms and Jews

288
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:52,920
need an escape more than ever,

289
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:54,760
Britain issues a white paper.

290
00:11:54,760 --> 00:11:58,280
It caps Jewish immigration at 75,000 over five years,

291
00:11:58,280 --> 00:12:00,320
then ends it unless Arabs agree.

292
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:02,960
The door closes at the worst possible moment.

293
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:06,440
What happens next is the darkest chapter in Jewish history

294
00:12:06,440 --> 00:12:08,160
and it should be told plainly.

295
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:11,520
In 1933, the Nazis take power in Germany.

296
00:12:11,520 --> 00:12:15,760
Step by step, Jews are stripped of citizenship, jobs and homes.

297
00:12:15,760 --> 00:12:18,720
In November 1938, on Kristallnacht,

298
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:20,800
Synagogues burn across Germany.

299
00:12:20,800 --> 00:12:23,560
Then comes war and in 1941,

300
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:26,440
mass shootings behind the German lines in the east.

301
00:12:26,440 --> 00:12:29,160
By 1942, the Nazis are running death camps

302
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:33,200
with gas chambers built to murder Jews on an industrial scale.

303
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:36,440
Six million Jewish men, women and children were killed.

304
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:38,720
About two out of every three Jews in Europe,

305
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:42,200
whole communities in Poland, Lithuania, Greece, Hungary,

306
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:42,960
simply gone.

307
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:47,000
Some resist in the Warsaw ghetto uprising in 1943

308
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:49,280
and in the forest as partisans.

309
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:52,520
Some neighbors hide Jews at the risk of their own lives.

310
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:55,560
But most countries, including the United States and Britain,

311
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:58,120
keep their doors mostly closed to refugees.

312
00:12:58,120 --> 00:13:00,480
The Nazis murder millions of others too.

313
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:03,800
Roma, Poles, Soviet prisoners, disabled people.

314
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:06,480
When the camps are liberated in 1945,

315
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:08,520
survivors have nowhere to go.

316
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:11,000
Their villages are empty or hostile.

317
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,680
About a quarter of a million Jews

318
00:13:12,680 --> 00:13:16,040
wait in displaced persons camps, sometimes for years.

319
00:13:16,040 --> 00:13:18,240
Some try to reach Palestine on crowded,

320
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:21,080
rickety ships past a British naval blockade.

321
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:25,880
In 1947, the ship Exodus, carrying over 4,000 survivors,

322
00:13:25,880 --> 00:13:29,280
is intercepted and the passengers are sent back to Germany.

323
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:31,520
The world sees it and for many people,

324
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:34,800
a question that had been political becomes a moral one.

325
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:37,920
Where exactly are these people supposed to go?

326
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:42,160
Britain, exhausted, hands the problem to the new United Nations.

327
00:13:42,160 --> 00:13:46,400
On November 29, 1947, the UN votes to divide Palestine

328
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:48,560
into a Jewish state and an Arab state

329
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:51,360
with Jerusalem under international control.

330
00:13:51,360 --> 00:13:55,120
33 countries vote yes, 13 no, 10 abstain.

331
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:58,200
The Jewish leadership accepts with reservations.

332
00:13:58,200 --> 00:14:00,040
The Arab leaders reject it.

333
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:02,160
They argue that it gives the Jewish minority

334
00:14:02,160 --> 00:14:04,880
about a third of the people more than half the land

335
00:14:04,880 --> 00:14:07,480
and that nobody asks the people who lived there.

336
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:09,680
Civil war begins the next day.

337
00:14:09,680 --> 00:14:12,800
In the months that follow, atrocities happen on both sides.

338
00:14:12,800 --> 00:14:15,560
In April, at the village of Deir Yassin,

339
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:18,880
Jewish irregulars kill over 100 Arab villagers.

340
00:14:18,880 --> 00:14:21,400
Days later, Arab fighters ambush a convoy

341
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:23,240
heading to Hadassah Hospital

342
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:26,960
and kill 78 Jewish doctors, nurses and others.

343
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:30,040
Fear drives people out of their homes on both sides.

344
00:14:30,040 --> 00:14:33,040
On May 14, 1948, David Ben Gurion

345
00:14:33,040 --> 00:14:34,880
stands in a Tel Aviv Museum

346
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:37,560
and reads the Declaration of the State of Israel.

347
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:40,000
Within minutes, the United States recognizes it.

348
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:43,120
The next day, the armies of Egypt, Jordan, Syria, Iraq

349
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:44,560
and Lebanon invade.

350
00:14:44,560 --> 00:14:47,960
Israelis call what follows the war of independence.

351
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:50,560
Palestinians call what happens to them the Nakba,

352
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:51,800
the catastrophe.

353
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:53,800
Both names describe real things.

354
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:55,400
Israel survives the invasion

355
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:58,440
and ends up with more land than the UN plan gave it.

356
00:14:58,440 --> 00:15:03,440
When the fighting stops in 1949, about 700,000 Palestinians,

357
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:06,600
most of the Arabs who lived in what became Israel

358
00:15:06,600 --> 00:15:09,280
have fled or been driven from their homes.

359
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:12,480
Historians still argue about how many ran from the fighting

360
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:15,920
and how many were expelled, but they agree on the outcome.

361
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:18,080
Israel does not let them return.

362
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:20,760
They and their descendants, millions of people today

363
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:23,000
are still counted as refugees.

364
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,520
Jordan takes the West Bank,

365
00:15:24,520 --> 00:15:26,920
including East Jerusalem and the Old City

366
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:29,160
and Jews are expelled from the Old City

367
00:15:29,160 --> 00:15:31,680
and kept from the Western Wall for 19 years.

368
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:33,120
Egypt takes Gaza.

369
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:37,480
Inside Israel, about 150,000 Palestinians stay

370
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:39,440
and become Israeli citizens,

371
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:43,000
though they live under military rule until 1966.

372
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:46,080
In 1950, Israel passes the law of return,

373
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:47,760
which gives any Jew in the world the right

374
00:15:47,760 --> 00:15:49,920
to immigrate and become a citizen.

375
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:52,440
Palestinian refugees have no such right.

376
00:15:52,440 --> 00:15:55,160
At the same time, another exodus is underway.

377
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:59,840
Over the next few decades, around 850,000 Jews leave

378
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:02,760
or are pushed out of Arab countries and Iran.

379
00:16:02,760 --> 00:16:05,600
Iraq, Yemen, Morocco, Egypt, Libya.

380
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:07,480
Their property is often seized.

381
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:09,840
About 600,000 settle in Israel,

382
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:12,360
a country that had 700,000 people

383
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:15,240
and that now doubles in size in just a few years,

384
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:17,560
housing newcomers in tent camps.

385
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:19,520
Today, roughly half of Israel's Jews

386
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:22,280
trace their roots to the Middle East and North Africa,

387
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:24,640
so the war ends with two refugee peoples,

388
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:26,960
two founding stories and no peace.

389
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:29,880
Not one Arab state recognizes Israel.

390
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:32,680
In the 1950s, border raids by Palestinians

391
00:16:32,680 --> 00:16:35,440
and Israeli reprisals turn into a cycle.

392
00:16:35,440 --> 00:16:38,080
In 1956, Israel joins Britain and France

393
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:40,520
in attacking Egypt over the Suez Canal

394
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:42,440
and is pressured to withdraw.

395
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:44,760
By 1967, tension peaks.

396
00:16:44,760 --> 00:16:46,040
Egypt's president, Nasser,

397
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:48,600
expels United Nations peacekeepers from Sinai,

398
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:50,160
moves troops to the border

399
00:16:50,160 --> 00:16:53,200
and closes the Straits of Tiran to Israeli ships.

400
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:55,200
Israel calls that an act of war.

401
00:16:55,200 --> 00:16:57,560
On June 5th, Israel strikes first,

402
00:16:57,560 --> 00:17:00,040
destroying most of Egypt's air force on the ground

403
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:01,160
within hours.

404
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:03,920
In six days, Israel takes the Sinai and Gaza

405
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:06,240
from Egypt, the West Bank and East Jerusalem

406
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:08,960
from Jordan and the Golan Heights from Syria.

407
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:11,280
Israeli soldiers weep at the Western Wall,

408
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:14,480
which Jews had not been able to reach since 48.

409
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:17,320
For many Jews, it feels like a miracle.

410
00:17:17,320 --> 00:17:18,560
For the million Palestinians

411
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:20,600
now under Israeli military control,

412
00:17:20,600 --> 00:17:22,120
it is the start of an occupation

413
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:23,760
that has lasted ever since.

414
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:25,840
Israel annexes East Jerusalem

415
00:17:25,840 --> 00:17:28,200
and offers its Palestinian residents residency,

416
00:17:28,200 --> 00:17:32,320
not citizenship, which most of the world does not recognize.

417
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:34,280
And Israelis still argue among themselves

418
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:38,640
about whether 67 was a war of necessity or a war of choice.

419
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:40,640
The Arab League answers at Khartoum

420
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:44,160
with the famous three noes: no peace, no recognition,

421
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:45,880
no negotiation with Israel.

422
00:17:45,880 --> 00:17:49,400
Israel begins building settlements in the occupied land.

423
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:51,240
Most countries consider them illegal

424
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:53,080
under international law.

425
00:17:53,080 --> 00:17:56,240
Israeli governments dispute that. Through the early 70s,

426
00:17:56,240 --> 00:17:58,480
Palestinian groups led by the PLO

427
00:17:58,480 --> 00:18:01,240
carry out hijackings and attacks abroad.

428
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:03,680
At the 1972 Olympics in Munich,

429
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:07,000
gunmen kill 11 Israeli athletes and coaches.

430
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:09,920
Then on October 6th, 1973,

431
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:12,760
Yom Kippur, the holiest day in the Jewish calendar,

432
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:15,360
Egypt and Syria attacked by surprise.

433
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:16,960
For a few days, Israel reels

434
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:19,240
and about 2,600 of its soldiers died

435
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:21,040
before it turns the tide.

436
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:25,480
In 1976, Israeli commandos fly 4,000 kilometers

437
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:28,960
to Entebbe, Uganda, and rescue more than 100 hostages

438
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:30,560
from a hijacked plane.

439
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:33,960
But the shock of 73 shatters Israel's confidence

440
00:18:33,960 --> 00:18:36,280
and it changes something in Egypt's president,

441
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:37,440
Anwar Sadat.

442
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:41,240
In 1977, he does what no Arab leader has done.

443
00:18:41,240 --> 00:18:44,720
He flies to Jerusalem and speaks to the Israeli parliament.

444
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:47,400
In 1979, after talks at Camp David,

445
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:49,840
Egypt and Israel sign a peace treaty.

446
00:18:49,840 --> 00:18:53,520
Israel returns the Sinai, Egypt recognizes Israel.

447
00:18:53,520 --> 00:18:57,120
Sadat is assassinated by Islamist soldiers two years later.

448
00:18:57,120 --> 00:18:59,400
But the peace holds to this day.

449
00:18:59,400 --> 00:19:02,040
And it proves that land can be traded for peace.

450
00:19:02,040 --> 00:19:04,080
Whether that could work with the Palestinians

451
00:19:04,080 --> 00:19:07,160
is the question that dominates the next 40 years.

452
00:19:07,160 --> 00:19:11,320
In 1982, Israel invades Lebanon to drive out the PLO

453
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:14,720
and ends up occupying the south of the country for 18 years.

454
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:17,160
Out of that occupation grows a new enemy,

455
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:19,080
Hezbollah backed by Iran.

456
00:19:19,080 --> 00:19:22,200
Then in 1987, a Palestinian uprising

457
00:19:22,200 --> 00:19:23,800
begins in Gaza and spreads.

458
00:19:23,800 --> 00:19:27,440
The First Intifada, mostly stones, strikes and clashes

459
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:29,560
met by heavy Israeli force.

460
00:19:29,560 --> 00:19:31,840
Both sides strangely are exhausted.

461
00:19:31,840 --> 00:19:34,480
In 1993, secret talks in Oslo lead

462
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:36,640
to a famous handshake on the White House lawn

463
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:39,280
between Israel's prime minister Yitzhak Rabin

464
00:19:39,280 --> 00:19:42,240
and the Palestinian leader Yasser Arafat.

465
00:19:42,240 --> 00:19:44,800
Israel and the PLO recognize each other.

466
00:19:44,800 --> 00:19:46,640
A Palestinian authority is created

467
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:49,120
to govern parts of the West Bank and Gaza,

468
00:19:49,120 --> 00:19:51,720
while the hardest questions are left for later,

469
00:19:51,720 --> 00:19:54,640
Jerusalem, borders, refugees, settlements.

470
00:19:54,640 --> 00:19:57,000
Then the opponents on both sides go to work.

471
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,000
Hamas, a Palestinian Islamist group

472
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,920
that rejects Israel's existence,

473
00:20:00,920 --> 00:20:03,280
sends suicide bombers onto Israeli buses

474
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:04,480
and into cafes.

475
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:06,880
And on November 4th, 1995,

476
00:20:06,880 --> 00:20:09,120
Rabin is assassinated at a peace rally

477
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:12,240
by a Jewish Israeli extremist who opposed the deal.

478
00:20:12,240 --> 00:20:14,880
In 2000, talks at Camp David Collapse

479
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:17,080
and each side blames the other.

480
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:18,680
The Second Intifada begins,

481
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:22,000
five years of suicide bombings and military crackdowns

482
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,840
in which about a thousand Israelis

483
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:26,760
and more than 3,000 Palestinians are killed.

484
00:20:26,760 --> 00:20:29,840
Israel builds a barrier in and around the West Bank,

485
00:20:29,840 --> 00:20:32,200
which it says stops the bombers

486
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:34,800
which Palestinians say seizes their land.

487
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:37,640
In 2005, Israel pulls all its settlers

488
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:39,200
and soldiers out of Gaza.

489
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:41,680
Two years later, Hamas takes control of Gaza

490
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:44,640
after a brief civil war with its rival Fatah

491
00:20:44,640 --> 00:20:46,760
and Israel and Egypt blockade the territory.

492
00:20:46,760 --> 00:20:50,080
Rockets from Gaza, Israeli air strikes on Gaza,

493
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:54,440
wars in 2008, 12, 14 and 21.

494
00:20:54,440 --> 00:20:55,800
Meanwhile in the West Bank,

495
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:57,840
Israeli settlement keeps growing.

496
00:20:57,840 --> 00:21:00,880
Today about half a million Israeli settlers live there

497
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:04,040
and roughly 200,000 more in East Jerusalem.

498
00:21:04,040 --> 00:21:07,120
Most of the world considers the settlements illegal.

499
00:21:07,120 --> 00:21:09,120
Israeli governments dispute that

500
00:21:09,120 --> 00:21:10,600
and many settlers see themselves

501
00:21:10,600 --> 00:21:13,080
as returning to the biblical heartland.

502
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:16,480
Palestinians in the West Bank live under a patchwork

503
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:18,800
of Palestinian and Israeli control.

504
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:21,840
A two-state solution still has supporters on both sides

505
00:21:21,840 --> 00:21:24,920
but too many it feels further away every year.

506
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:27,840
And yet in 2020 something unexpected,

507
00:21:27,840 --> 00:21:31,760
the Abraham Accords, the United Arab Emirates

508
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:34,160
and Bahrain, then Morocco and Sudan

509
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:35,880
normalized relations with Israel

510
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:38,440
without any deal for the Palestinians.

511
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:40,240
Many governments in the region have decided

512
00:21:40,240 --> 00:21:41,840
that Iran is the bigger threat

513
00:21:41,840 --> 00:21:44,240
and that the Palestinian question can wait.

514
00:21:44,240 --> 00:21:46,120
Palestinians feel forgotten.

515
00:21:46,120 --> 00:21:49,920
Israel in early 2023 is deeply divided

516
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:54,160
with months of mass protests over a plan to weaken the courts.

517
00:21:54,160 --> 00:21:57,360
Then on the morning of October 7th, 2023,

518
00:21:57,360 --> 00:21:59,200
a Saturday and a Jewish holiday,

519
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:02,560
Hamas led fighters break through the Gaza border fence.

520
00:22:02,560 --> 00:22:06,200
They kill about 1200 people, most of them civilians

521
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:08,960
in farming communities and at a music festival,

522
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:11,200
it is the deadliest single day for Jews

523
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:12,720
since the Holocaust.

524
00:22:12,720 --> 00:22:16,600
And they take 251 people hostage into Gaza.

525
00:22:16,600 --> 00:22:19,160
Israel declares war on Hamas.

526
00:22:19,160 --> 00:22:21,560
The campaign that follows is the most destructive

527
00:22:21,560 --> 00:22:22,720
in Gaza's history.

528
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:24,520
According to Gaza's health ministry,

529
00:22:24,520 --> 00:22:26,480
part of the Hamas run government,

530
00:22:26,480 --> 00:22:29,600
more than 74,000 Palestinians have been killed

531
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:32,440
about half of them women and children.

532
00:22:32,440 --> 00:22:35,600
The ministry does not separate civilians from fighters.

533
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:39,120
UN agencies generally consider its counts reliable.

534
00:22:39,120 --> 00:22:40,240
Israel disputes them.

535
00:22:40,240 --> 00:22:43,280
Most of Gaza's two million people have been displaced,

536
00:22:43,280 --> 00:22:44,880
many of them more than once

537
00:22:44,880 --> 00:22:48,200
and much of its housing, hospitals and water systems

538
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:49,160
are destroyed.

539
00:22:49,160 --> 00:22:50,920
Israel says it is fighting an enemy

540
00:22:50,920 --> 00:22:52,760
that hides among civilians

541
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:54,920
and that its goal is to destroy Hamas

542
00:22:54,920 --> 00:22:56,560
and bring the hostages home.

543
00:22:56,560 --> 00:22:58,400
Its critics say the cost to civilians

544
00:22:58,400 --> 00:23:01,360
is far beyond what any goal can justify.

545
00:23:01,360 --> 00:23:04,200
Courts and scholars are still weighing the gravest charges

546
00:23:04,200 --> 00:23:06,440
and a film cannot settle that for them.

547
00:23:06,440 --> 00:23:08,000
The war spreads.

548
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:10,840
Hezbollah in Lebanon fires on Northern Israel

549
00:23:10,840 --> 00:23:14,440
and in 2024, Israel and Hezbollah fight a war

550
00:23:14,440 --> 00:23:17,200
that ends in a ceasefire that November.

551
00:23:17,200 --> 00:23:20,760
In June 2025, Israel and Iran trade strikes

552
00:23:20,760 --> 00:23:22,920
for 12 days with the United States

553
00:23:22,920 --> 00:23:25,760
joining in against Iran's nuclear sites.

554
00:23:25,760 --> 00:23:28,840
In October 2025, after two years of war,

555
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:31,520
a ceasefire brokered by the United States takes hold

556
00:23:31,520 --> 00:23:33,800
and the remaining hostages are returned.

557
00:23:33,800 --> 00:23:36,760
But a year later, its hardest parts are stuck.

558
00:23:36,760 --> 00:23:39,440
Who governs Gaza, whether Hamas disarms

559
00:23:39,440 --> 00:23:41,360
and when Israeli forces withdraw?

560
00:23:41,360 --> 00:23:44,880
Most people in Gaza are still living in tents and rubble

561
00:23:44,880 --> 00:23:48,360
and in Israel, an election in October, 2026

562
00:23:48,360 --> 00:23:50,440
has left the political picture unsettled

563
00:23:50,480 --> 00:23:51,800
as this is written.

564
00:23:51,800 --> 00:23:53,600
So where does that leave us?

565
00:23:53,600 --> 00:23:56,960
Israel today is a country of about 10 million people.

566
00:23:56,960 --> 00:23:59,880
Roughly three in four are Jewish and about one in five

567
00:23:59,880 --> 00:24:00,720
is Arab.

568
00:24:00,720 --> 00:24:02,880
The world has about 15 million Jews

569
00:24:02,880 --> 00:24:04,600
with Israel and the United States

570
00:24:04,600 --> 00:24:06,800
each home to six or seven million.

571
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:09,360
Millions of Palestinians live in the West Bank

572
00:24:09,360 --> 00:24:12,320
in Gaza and in Jordan, Lebanon and beyond.

573
00:24:12,320 --> 00:24:14,360
Remember the question from the beginning,

574
00:24:14,360 --> 00:24:16,960
why does almost nobody have the whole story

575
00:24:16,960 --> 00:24:19,200
because it is two true stories?

576
00:24:19,200 --> 00:24:22,040
One is about a people who were driven from their home,

577
00:24:22,040 --> 00:24:24,320
scattered, hunted, nearly erased

578
00:24:24,320 --> 00:24:26,160
and who rebuilt a country in a land

579
00:24:26,160 --> 00:24:28,480
they never stopped praying toward.

580
00:24:28,480 --> 00:24:31,560
The other is about a people who were living on that land

581
00:24:31,560 --> 00:24:35,160
whose homes and villages were lost in the making of that country

582
00:24:35,160 --> 00:24:37,320
and who still have no state of their own.

583
00:24:37,320 --> 00:24:40,000
Each story is true and for the people who live it,

584
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:42,240
each one is a story of survival.

585
00:24:42,240 --> 00:24:46,360
4,000 years ago, a man walked into Canaan with a promise.

586
00:24:46,360 --> 00:24:48,600
A people lost their home, kept their book

587
00:24:48,640 --> 00:24:50,360
and found each other again.

588
00:24:50,360 --> 00:24:52,640
Another people have held on to their homes,

589
00:24:52,640 --> 00:24:56,320
their keys and their names through exile and occupation.

590
00:24:56,320 --> 00:24:59,120
Whether those two stories can be lived side by side

591
00:24:59,120 --> 00:25:01,480
is the one page nobody has written yet.
